codex-multi-account
===================

This project is a derivative work of `claude-multi-account`
(https://github.com/Loopsmiths-labs/claude-multi-account), which is
distributed under the MIT License. The original copyright notice and license
text are preserved in `LICENSE`.

What was carried over from the original project
-----------------------------------------------
* The product concept: a terminal-first, user-controlled multi-account manager
  for an AI coding CLI.
* The interaction model: a numbered account picker, a persistent "active
  account" pointer, and a launcher that starts the vendor CLI with the
  selected account's credentials.
* The core insight that account isolation and conversation history are
  separable concerns, so a session created under one account can be resumed
  under another.

What is new here
----------------
* An architecture built around the OpenAI Codex CLI's actual `CODEX_HOME`
  layout (auth.json, config.toml, sessions/, state_*.sqlite,
  thread_history_*.sqlite), rather than Claude Code's `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`.
* Credential materialisation with write-back, ownership tracking and atomic
  file replacement, instead of static per-account config directories.
* Cross-process locking, writer registration and stale-lock recovery.
* A TypeScript codebase with lint, typecheck, unit, integration and smoke
  test coverage.

Third-party software
--------------------
`codex-multi-account` does not vendor, patch or redistribute the OpenAI Codex
CLI. It invokes the user's own installation of `@openai/codex` (Apache-2.0) as
an external process. "OpenAI", "ChatGPT" and "Codex" are trademarks of OpenAI;
